---
const { id } = Astro.props;
---

<section id={id} class="border-t border-border pt-12 lg:pt-24 pb-12 lg:pb-24 bg-background">
  <div class="px-4 md:px-6 lg:max-w-4xl mx-auto flex flex-col gap-6">
    <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-light tracking-tight text-foreground leading-tight">
      APSC, UPSC &amp; ADRE Coaching in Guwahati — <span class="text-primary italic">What We Cover</span>
    </h2>
    <p class="text-muted-foreground font-light leading-relaxed">
      Takshasheela School of Civil Services provides complete preparation for
      the <strong class="text-foreground font-semibold">APSC Combined Competitive Examination (CCE)</strong>, the
      <strong class="text-foreground font-semibold">UPSC Civil Services Examination</strong> and the
      <strong class="text-foreground font-semibold">Assam Direct Recruitment Exam (ADRE)</strong> from our centre in
      Guwahati and through live online classes across Assam and the Northeast.
    </p>
    <p class="text-muted-foreground font-light leading-relaxed">
      Our APSC CCE programme covers the full Prelims and Mains syllabus —
      Indian History, Polity and Governance, Geography, Economy, Science &amp;
      Technology, Environment, Ethics and Current Affairs — along with the
      Assam-specific portions that decide ranks:
      <strong class="text-foreground font-semibold">Assam History</strong>, <strong class="text-foreground font-semibold">Assam Geography and Polity</strong>,
      <strong class="text-foreground font-semibold">Assam Art &amp; Culture</strong> and the
      <strong class="text-foreground font-semibold">Assam Year Book</strong>. CSAT preparation, answer-writing
      practice for Mains, and previous year question analysis are built into
      every batch.
    </p>
    <p class="text-muted-foreground font-light leading-relaxed">
      Our UPSC batches follow the same rigour for the Civil Services
      Examination, with dedicated coverage of General Studies Papers I–IV,
      CSAT, Essay and Optional subjects, plus structured mains answer-writing
      and mock interview practice for aspirants targeting the IAS, IPS and
      allied services. For state government aspirants, our ADRE batches focus
      on the Assam Direct Recruitment Exam syllabus for Class III and Class IV
      posts, with daily practice tests and updated study material.
    </p>
    <p class="text-muted-foreground font-light leading-relaxed">
      Classes run in both <strong class="text-foreground font-semibold">online and offline modes</strong>, with
      recorded lectures available for revision, a monthly current affairs
      magazine, an advanced library, and regular full-length and sectional
      mock tests with individual feedback. Faculty with 5–20 years of
      experience from Delhi and across India mentor every batch, making
      Takshasheela one of the most complete options for civil services
      preparation in Guwahati.
    </p>
    <p class="text-muted-foreground font-light leading-relaxed">
      Whether you are appearing for the APSC CCE Prelims for the first time,
      preparing for UPSC Mains after clearing Prelims, or targeting an ADRE
      Class III or Class IV post, our mentors help you build a personalised
      study plan, track your progress through periodic assessments, and
      refine your answer-writing and interview skills before exam day.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
